/**

@page page_toolbox_loadbalancing_api_api_postprocessing Postprocessing of load balancing data

There are multiple postprocessing scripts shipped with the toolbox.
All of them use instances of OutputFile to parse a text file as written 
by Peano and then dump this information into various outputs.
All of them rely on the fact that you have the logging switched on for 
the toolbox, and there are lines in the file with the trace
```toolbox::loadbalancing::dumpStatistics```, i.e. trace information
has to be there as well.


- ```plot_load_distribution.py``` provides a plot of the load distribution over 
  time and hence yields plots similar to 

  @image html src/toolbox/loadbalancing/runtime_analysis_loadbalancing_example00.png

  This type of visualisation is particularly helpful whenever we have dynamic 
  load balancing and want to understand how the cells evolve over time. 
  Apparently, the plot above does not employ dynamic rebalancing and hence is a
  pretty bad example for this script.

- The @ref benchmarks_exahype2_ccz4_single_black "Schwarzschild black hole benchmark" 
  is shipped with a script which employs the load balancing parser to distill some 
  domain-specific knowledge. It can serve as a baseline of other tailored scripts
  producing outputs similar to
  
  @image html benchmarks/exahype2/ccz4/single-black-hole/trees-vs-runtime.png
   
*/
